  "title": "Improving soil structure of an arable crop farm in the district of Heilbronn (Germany)",
  "summary": "The Heilbronn pilot farm faces several climate challenges: increased temperatures, drought, and heavy precipitation. As part of LIFE AgriAdapt, the farm has adopted adaptation measures focusing on improving its soil structure. This includes using new crop management techniques, and better adapted varieties. In the framework of the LIFE AgriAdapt project, more than 120 pilot farms are testing sustainable adaptation measures to enhance the farm resilience to climate change, reduce greenhouse gas emissions and improve the farm competitiveness.",
